<<~ ahu slot=`#/purpose`>>

`projectingLeg` weighs the records' render, the base at the file's path and the disk through `decideProjection`, then pends a vanished file, pins a congruent agreement, or hands a file a hand moved to the island's capture door (`captureMoved`). A captured file's base moves to its bytes and the carrier marks for one more reading; a refused capture writes nothing over the file and rides `onRefusal`. Nothing holds between readings. It answers whether the flush writes. The DAM checklist (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/disk-projector-dam`>>) carries its observations.

<<~/ahu>>

